SUMMARY:Candlelight Fridays (Original Music by Steve Flemming) (Nov. 20th)
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nGood day everyone\,\
 n\nJoin me for the very first **Candlelight Fridays at The Pheasant**\, an
  intimate evening of original music\, storytelling and friendly company in
  a warm\, cozy pub setting.\n\nI'll be sharing a selection of songs I've w
 ritten over the years\, ranging from heartfelt folk and country ballads to
  soulful melodies\, rock and playful satire. My songs are filled with char
 acters searching for love\, navigating life's ups and downs\, questioning 
 the world around them and sometimes simply laughing at its absurdities.\n\
 nAlong the way\, I'll share a few personal stories about what inspired the
  songs and how they came to life.\n\nSo come grab a drink\, enjoy some din
 ner\, settle in by candlelight and see where the music takes us!\n\n*We'll
  also be joined by members of my other social group\, so there'll be plent
 y of friendly company to enjoy the evening with!*\n\n**Event Details:**\n\
 n**Candlelight Fridays**\n*(Original Music by Steve Flemming)*\n\n**Curiou
 s about the music?** Listen to some of my original songs on YouTube for a 
 little taste of the music I'll be sharing throughout the evening!\n[https:
 //www.youtube.com/@SteveFlemmingSongs](https://www.youtube.com/@SteveFlemm
 ingSongs)\n\nHere's what you can look forward to:\n\n* An evening of origi
 nal folk\, country\, soft rock\, duets and soulful music.\n* Personal stor
 ies and inspiration behind selected songs.\n* A relaxed\, candlelit pub at
 mosphere with dinner and drinks available.\n* Friendly conversation and th
 e opportunity to connect with fellow music lovers.\n\n**Where to Find Us?*
 *\n\nWe'll be gathering in the **back dining area** at **The Pheasant: A F
 irkin Pub**\, located at 1999 Avenue Road\, approximately six blocks north
  of Lawrence Avenue and south of Highway 401.\nIf you're unsure where to g
 o\, simply ask the bartender or wait staff for **Steve's event**. They'll 
 be happy to direct you.\n\n**Admission:**\nThis first evening is **free to
  attend!**\nIf you enjoy the music and would like to help support future e
 venings\, there'll be a small tip jar available. Contributions are entirel
 y optional and sincerely appreciated\, but most importantly\, I'm happy to
  have you there!\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n* Please arrive anytime aft
 er **6:30 p.m.**\n* The Pheasant offers a great dinner menu\, along with f
 ood and drink specials.\n* A minimum purchase of one beverage or appetizer
  per person is requested to help support the venue.\n\n**Parking and Trans
 portation:**\nThere's street parking along Avenue Road\, as well as free p
 arking on nearby residential side streets where permitted.\nThe venue is a
 pproximately a 15–20-minute walk from Yonge and Lawrence subway station.
  Alternatively\, you can take a bus or Uber from the station.\n\n**About S
 teve Flemming:**\nSteve Flemming is a Canadian songwriter and producer who
 se original folk\, country and story songs explore love\, longing\, everyd
 ay life and the deeper questions of being human. His writing brings togeth
 er vivid characters\, emotional honesty and an enduring curiosity about th
 e lives we lead. As lyricist and producer\, Steve shapes each song's story
 \, atmosphere and creative direction\, aiming to bring as much life as pos
 sible into every song.\n\nI hope you'll join me for what promises to be a 
 relaxing and enjoyable Friday evening of music\, stories and good company.
 \n\nLooking forward to seeing you at The Pheasant!\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve
  Flemming\n(Songwriter / Producer / Host)
