SUMMARY:After Dark Fridays (Original Music by Steve Flemming) (Nov. 20th) 
  
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nGood day everyone\,\
 n\nJoin me for the very first **After Dark Fridays at The Pheasant**\, a l
 ively Friday night of upbeat original music\, entertaining stories and gre
 at company in a warm\, welcoming pub setting.\n\nI'll be sharing a selecti
 on of songs I've written over the years\, with an emphasis on my more upbe
 at\, rhythmic and energetic music. From catchy country-rock and soulful gr
 ooves to playful satire\, lively duets and songs filled with humour\, ther
 e's plenty of variety to keep the evening interesting and entertaining.\n\
 nMy songs are filled with colourful characters\, unexpected twists\, refle
 ctions on love and relationships\, and observations about the sometimes wo
 nderful\, sometimes absurd world we live in.\n\nAlong the way\, I'll share
  a few personal stories about what inspired the songs and how they came to
  life.\n\nSo grab a drink\, enjoy some dinner\, meet some friendly people 
 and settle in for a fun Friday night of original music\, laughter and good
  company!\n\n*We'll also be joined by members of my other social group\, s
 o there'll be plenty of friendly company to enjoy the evening with!*\n\n**
 Event Details:**\n\n**After Dark Fridays**\n*(Original Music by Steve Flem
 ming)*\n\n**Curious about the music?** Listen to some of my original songs
  on YouTube for a little taste of the music I'll be sharing throughout the
  evening!\n\n[https://www.youtube.com/@SteveFlemmingSongs](https://www.you
 tube.com/@SteveFlemmingSongs)\n\nHere's what you can look forward to:\n\n*
  An evening of upbeat original country-rock\, soulful music\, lively duets
  and playful satire.\n* Personal stories\, humour and inspiration behind s
 elected songs.\n* A fun\, relaxed pub atmosphere with dinner and drinks av
 ailable.\n* Friendly conversation\, mingling and the opportunity to connec
 t with fellow music lovers.\n\n**Where to Find Us?**\n\nWe'll be gathering
  in the **back dining area** at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub**\, located a
 t 1999 Avenue Road\, approximately six blocks north of Lawrence Avenue and
  south of Highway 401.\n\nIf you're unsure where to go\, simply ask the ba
 rtender or wait staff for **Steve's event**. They'll be happy to direct yo
 u.\n\n**Admission:**\n\nThis first evening is **free to attend!**\n\nIf yo
 u enjoy the music and would like to help support future evenings\, there'l
 l be a small tip jar available. Contributions are entirely optional and si
 ncerely appreciated\, but most importantly\, I'm happy to have you there!\
 n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n* Please arrive anytime after **9:00 p.m.**\
 n* The Pheasant offers a great dinner menu\, along with food and drink spe
 cials.\n* A minimum purchase of one beverage or appetizer per person is re
 quested to help support the venue.\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\nT
 here's street parking along Avenue Road\, as well as free parking on nearb
 y residential side streets where permitted.\n\nThe venue is approximately 
 a 15–20-minute walk from Yonge and Lawrence subway station. Alternativel
 y\, you can take a bus or Uber from the station.\n\n**About Steve Flemming
 :**\n\nSteve Flemming is a Canadian songwriter and producer whose original
  folk\, country and story songs explore love\, longing\, everyday life and
  the deeper questions of being human. His writing brings together vivid ch
 aracters\, emotional honesty and an enduring curiosity about the lives we 
 lead. As lyricist and producer\, Steve shapes each song's story\, atmosphe
 re and creative direction\, aiming to bring as much life as possible into 
 every song.\n\nI hope you'll join me for what promises to be a fun and enj
 oyable Friday night of upbeat music\, entertaining stories and great compa
 ny.\n\nLooking forward to seeing you at The Pheasant!\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSt
 eve Flemming\n(Songwriter / Producer / Host)
